{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/810402-how-can-a-beast-pollute-things","id":810402,"title":"How can a beast pollute things?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-16T16:59:07-08:00","id":810402,"title":"How can a beast pollute things?","content":"One of the example Beasts is a Namtaru ravager who pollutes areas with fungus. I'm looking to play a variant of that concept with a splash of The Last of Us, but I can't figure out how to actually pollute places or objects in the mechanics. Everything the beast has to offer is scene long... and it isn't about *destroying* a person's home, it's about making their home inhospitable so they make the choice to leave.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if this can somehow be done with an object. A collector who doesn't steal things so much as make an item so hazardous to one's health that the owner better discard it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-16-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T19:41:23-08:00","id":810452,"title":"","content":"Most of what you'd be doing to pollute an area is less a matter of power usage, and more a matter of mundane labor. If memory serves, there's a Nightmare that allows you to plant other Nightmares into a victim to strike as needed, which could be used to fake an environmental disaster. It really depends on whether you want this Beast to actively engage in polluting, or just sit back and watch.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basilisk's Touch and Dragonfire are your best bets for taking a direct approach, as are piggybacking more major Lair Traits (Diseased, Noxious Fumes, or Toxic, to name a few) onto easier to simulate ones (Darkness, Exposed, Blazing Light). The best Nightmares for subtler, more long-term pollution are You Can't Wake Up or You Are Infected (best choice by far), comboed with Behold, My True Form!, Death Is a Prison, or Cursed Object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 01-16-2016, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T23:16:35-08:00","id":810501,"title":"","content":"Magically you can't. Mundanely, get a bag of toxic waste and start slathering it all over the insides of the local water treatment plant. Collect fungus, mix mustard gas, steal byproducts from chemical factories, et cetera.<br /> <br /> There are no mechanics for what happens when you fill someone's child's bedroom with black mold or manipulate assorted employees to arrange a nuclear meltdown near an urban center. It's not modeled. Talk to your ST and arrange something; you might not need to bring dice into it at all, though there are rules for poison that you could work from to model sicknesses like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:32:34-08:00","id":810636,"title":"","content":"Make friends with someone that the garou will try to gut you for exchanging basic pleasantries with. They usually have great ideas on that front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:00:46-08:00","id":810764,"title":"","content":"With a bit of reskinning, the Basilisk's Touch Atavism could do the job reasonably well. or you could tweak Dragonfire so that instead of fire damage it does poison damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:57:40-08:00","id":811174,"title":"","content":"Basilisk's Touch + Infestation will probably cover the whole &quot;being a fungus zombie monster&quot; part. The swarm thing in addition to Basilisk's touch is very nice mechanically as well.<br /> Your Teeth are Falling Out and You Must Obey covers the whole cordyceps thing.<br /> For lair traits... Probably Slick (can reproduce this with equipment by the same name) and Corrosive. Add on Diseased at Lair 2.<br /> <br /> It's really just figuring out how to handle the whole feeding thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-18-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:36:38-08:00","id":811439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/810402-how-can-a-beast-pollute-things?p=810636#post810636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make friends with someone that the garou will try to gut you for exchanging basic pleasantries with. They usually have great ideas on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank God Garou don't have to deal with Beasts....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:09:13-08:00","id":813120,"title":"","content":"So lets take a step back. If the answer isn't supernatural, what natural options are available to someone/a Beast to pollute an area? Particularly without owning an oil company for random oil spills. Some ideas off the top...<br /> <br /> * Stick decaying fish / etc. in someone's car.<br /> * Somehow encourage crime to move into an area.<br /> * Build businesses of ill repute in an area that wouldn't appreciate it.<br /> * Deface things of religious or symbolic significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-20-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}